// Core measures for Day 19. Paste each one into Power BI Desktop via Modeling > New measure.
// Table/column names assume the star schema: fact_home_values[home_value], fact_rent[rent],
// dim_date[Date] (marked as date table), dim_metro[RegionType]. NOT TESTED YET - verify with the checks at the bottom.
// Note: dim_metro and the fact views contain a 'country' row (United States). For rankings and averages
// put dim_metro[RegionType] = "msa" as a page/visual filter; select "United States" only for the national KPI.

// Average ZHVI home value for whatever metros/dates are in the current filter context
Avg Home Value = AVERAGE ( fact_home_values[home_value] )

// Average ZORI monthly rent for the current filter context
Avg Rent = AVERAGE ( fact_rent[rent] )

// Year-over-year % change in Avg Home Value (compares to the same date one year earlier; blank if no prior-year data)
YoY % =
VAR CurrentValue = [Avg Home Value]
VAR PriorValue =
    CALCULATE ( [Avg Home Value], DATEADD ( dim_date[Date], -1, YEAR ) )
RETURN
    DIVIDE ( CurrentValue - PriorValue, PriorValue )

// Gross annual rent as % of home value. Both averages use only metros that have BOTH rent and home value
// data in the current filter context, so the numerator and denominator cover the same metros.
Rent-to-Price =
VAR MetrosWithBoth =
    FILTER (
        dim_metro,
        CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( fact_rent ) ) > 0
            && CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( fact_home_values ) ) > 0
    )
RETURN
    DIVIDE (
        CALCULATE ( [Avg Rent], MetrosWithBoth ) * 12,
        CALCULATE ( [Avg Home Value], MetrosWithBoth )
    )

// ---- Verification (must match analysis.sql, latest month = Sep 2026) ----
// Slicer: dim_date = 2026-09-30
//  - Metro = United States:  YoY % = 1.19%   (Q1/Q7)
//  - Metro = Abilene, TX:    Avg Home Value = 221,508 | YoY % = 9.69% | Avg Rent = 1,990 | Rent-to-Price = 10.78%   (Q2/Q5)
//  - Metro = Galesburg, IL:  YoY % = 11.78%   (Q2)
// All metros (page filter dim_metro[RegionType] = "msa", dim_date = 2026-09-30), computed from SQL:
//  - Avg Home Value = 297,435 | YoY % = 2.22% (simple average of metros, so NOT the 1.19% national figure)
//  - Avg Rent = 1,498 (740 metros have rent that month) | Rent-to-Price = 5.59% (727 metros have both rent and home value)
//  - These are after the dim_metro fix (908 metros); refresh the model in Power BI first.
//  - If Rent-to-Price shows about 6.05%, the metro filter isn't working (denominator uses all 894 home-value metros)

// ---- Market measures (added 2026-11-19, Zillow only; README question 3) ----
// Model setup first: in Power BI, Get data > SQL Server > [Housing Data] > tick fact_market. Then in Model view:
//   fact_market[RegionID]   -> dim_metro[RegionID]  (many-to-one)
//   fact_market[month_date] -> dim_date[Date]       (many-to-one)
// inventory = homes for sale; days_to_pending = mean days for a listing to go under contract.

// Average for-sale inventory for the current filter context
Avg Inventory = AVERAGE ( fact_market[inventory] )

// Average days to pending for the current filter context (blank where Zillow has no figure)
Avg Days to Pending = AVERAGE ( fact_market[days_to_pending] )

// ---- Verification for the market measures (must match 06_fact_market.sql / the CSVs) ----
// Slicer: dim_date = 2026-09-30
//  - Metro = Atlanta, GA:  Avg Inventory = 33,948 | Avg Days to Pending = 72
// All metros (page filter dim_metro[RegionType] = "msa", dim_date = 2026-09-30):
//  - Avg Inventory = 1,401.7 (926 metros) | Avg Days to Pending = 58.1 (695 metros)
